# Tey Standards

`tey/standards` provides offline deployment configuration checks and optional, rule-tagged Pest architecture tests with an exact debt ratchet. Keep it in production `require`; architecture checks need Pest 4.7+ or Pest 5, the matching pest-plugin-arch 4.x or 5.x and PHP-Parser 5.x in `require-dev`.

Run `php artisan standards:preflight` before deploy migrations and stop on a nonzero exit. Use `--ci` to skip production-secret checks in CI and `--strict` to fail on failed warning-level checks. Advisory warnings remain non-blocking. A skipped check is not a pass.

Ship an app-owned favicon.svg, non-empty favicon.ico and 180×180 apple-touch-icon.png, linked in every root layout. `brand.favicon` reads files only and runs in CI; known Laravel defaults, a missing/empty ICO or no non-data icon link fail at warning level (exit 1 only under strict). Missing layout evidence is Unknown and advisory. Set `preflight.brand.layouts` to every root layout's base-relative path for additional shells or non-Inertia apps; otherwise inertia.root_view or app is inspected. `preflight.brand.known_default_hashes` adds SHA-256 defaults to reject.

CI follows rule 51: default-branch pushes, pull_request types opened/synchronize/reopened/ready_for_review, workflow/PR concurrency cancelling only PR runs, expensive jobs skipping drafts, and timeout-minutes on every job. Apps use Linux only on every event and one PHP version on PRs; extra PHP versions may run nightly/manually. Distributed packages (anything others install or run, including sold packages and generated output) test Windows on ready PRs before merge because others run them there; macOS is advisory, PHP matrices are exempt, and drafts may skip Windows. Pass ciDefaultBranches and ciDistribution from preflight.ci.default_branches and preflight.ci.distribution (PREFLIGHT_CI_DISTRIBUTION: app|package). Detection then uses Composer type (project → app, other types → package), artisan → app, else advisory Unknown with config instructions. Consolidate small jobs first: per-job rounding means 2m43s → 2m12s still bills three minutes; save below 2:00. Cache only above ~45 s cold or just over a minute boundary; measured 31 s → 26 s Setup plus ~5 s restore saved about zero against ±20 s noise. Uncached installs get advisory cache suggestions, never strict failures. CiTriggers::findings() feeds [rule 51] failures; advisories() separately reports cache/macOS/Unknown. ci.triggers is CI-only, skipped in deploy runs. Docs skipping, dynamic expressions, reusable workflows, wrapper scripts and required checks need manual review; use a changes job when paths-ignore would leave required checks pending.

Queues default to sync until needed, then the hosting platform's scale-to-zero managed queue (Laravel Cloud managed queues), never an always-on worker. `QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync` passes unless `preflight.queue.expect_worker` (`PREFLIGHT_QUEUE_EXPECT_WORKER`, nullable boolean, unset by default) is true. An async queue with that flag false warns. The names stay unchanged: “a worker” means whatever drains the queue, normally the managed queue. The checks remain driver-based. `queue.worker` alone reads queue storage, with at most one database query or Redis call under `preflight.timeout`; it skips in CI and never blocks, even under `--strict`. `preflight.queue.max_backlog_minutes` (`PREFLIGHT_QUEUE_MAX_BACKLOG_MINUTES`) defaults to 15. Old backlog warns; unavailable or unsupported evidence reports Unknown. Enable the hosting platform's managed queue for this connection or deliberately use sync for future jobs and review the backlog; switching connections does not move or drain existing jobs. The check sees the previous release's queue before migrate; it does not prove a worker exists or that this deploy broke anything. No heartbeat or hosting API check ships here.

Add ratchet entries explicitly to `Configuration::allowlist`: one exact `rule`, `target` and `check`, with a reason and a real `Y-m-d` date. Review the diagnostic before adding it. Never discover or generate exceptions from current violations at runtime. Fixed or deleted debt fails as stale; remove its entry.

For an app check, implement `Tey\Standards\Preflight\Check` with a unique lowercase dotted `name()`, a `Level`, `needsSecrets()` and `run(): Result`. Tag its class `standards.preflight` in a service provider, or call `Tey\Standards\Preflight::register(CheckClass::class)` with the active container. Register once, bound any network timeout, and keep secrets out of messages.

Traverse before you build: run `php artisan standards:pattern` (or the `pattern_lookup` MCP tool), answer its questions, and scaffold with the leaf's `standards:make` command. Stamp hand-written new files `standards-pattern: <leaf-id>`, or `gap` when no leaf fits. `php artisan standards:check --changed` must pass before every commit and push. Fix findings; add an allowlist entry (with reason and expires) only for reviewed debt.
